      "thinking": "I'm adding up the A column, which comes to roughly 869,000 across the twelve values, and I've started on column B by summing its first few figures.\n\nNow I'm checking the B, C and D column sums, which come to about 418,000, 495,000 and 86,000. Adding the four totals gives roughly 1.87 million, with A at about 46.5% and C at 26.5%. Comparing August to July, A and B both fell about 42-43%, while C and D each dropped around 31%.\n\n",
      "type": "thinking"
     },
     {
      "text": "Stamping (dept_a) is the most expensive department in every month, ahead of Painting (dept_c), Welding (dept_b) and Assembly (dept_d). Costs come from each department's own meter, with each 15\u2011minute interval priced at its tariff band.\n\n**Monthly electricity cost (EUR)**\n\n| Month | Stamping (A) | Welding (B) | Painting (C) | Assembly (D) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Nov 2025 | 72,990 | 34,799 | 41,301 | 7,175 |\n| Dec 2025 | 63,906 | 30,646 | 37,931 | 6,493 |\n| Jan 2026 | 67,165 | 32,535 | 39,712 | 6,867 |\n| Feb 2026 | 70,830 | 34,437 | 39,580 | 6,886 |\n| Mar 2026 | 78,301 | 37,658 | 43,804 | 7,581 |\n| Apr 2026 | 77,739 | 37,499 | 42,977 | 7,486 |\n| May 2026 | 75,532 | 36,406 | 43,206 | 7,473 |\n| Jun 2026 | 77,632 | 37,344 | 43,210 | 7,536 |\n| Jul 2026 | 81,106 | 39,128 | 44,689 | 7,744 |\n| Aug 2026 | 46,031 | 22,688 | 30,723 | 5,308 |\n| Sep 2026 | 78,230 | 37,324 | 43,245 | 7,534 |\n| Oct 2026 | 79,574 | 37,832 | 44,325 | 7,627 |\n| **Year (approx.)** | **~869,000** | **~418,300** | **~494,700** | **~85,700** |\n\n**What stands out**\n- **Ranking:** The order is the same every month: Stamping, then Painting, then Welding, then Assembly. Over the year, Stamping is about 46.5% of the total for the four departments, Painting about 26.5%, Welding about 22.4% and Assembly about 4.6%. The combined total is about \u20ac1.87M.\n- **Seasonal pattern:** Costs are lowest in December and January. They rise from March and peak in July for all four departments.\n- **August dip:** August is much lower everywhere. Compared with July, Stamping and Welding fall by about 42\u201343%, and Painting and Assembly by about 31%. The data doesn't say why; a summer shutdown is a plausible guess. Painting falls less than Stamping and Welding, so it seems to have more load that keeps running, such as its ovens.\n- Costs return to normal levels in September and October.",
